15678	{"artifactId":"HLD-c32aa60534232f36","entry":{"id":"review-546e9ef0197ecb78c3bc12fcb075384b","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-28T08:08:11.924Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The HLD's six Story boundaries (s1–s6, owning sc1/sc6, sc2, sc3, sc4, sc5, sc7) map 1:1 onto DEF-c32aa60534232f36's six Stories (s1 'Orient both review modes' through s6 'Adopt the new review mechanism') and preserve its five non-goals (no design-review replacement, no severity-policy change, no fixed-savings guarantee, no new usage warehouse/UI, no reconstruction of unpersisted legacy answers) via explicit HLD statements ('No new warehouse, pricing engine or usage arrays...', 'preserve legacy CR readers and design-document review behavior').","evidence":"DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json body.stories[0..5].id/title/dependsOn match HLD §6.1-6.6 exactly (s1 dependsOn [], s2 dependsOn [s1], s3 dependsOn [s1,s2], s4 dependsOn [s2,s3], s5 dependsOn [s2,s3,s4], s6 dependsOn all); DEF body.nonGoals[0..4] are each explicitly honored in HLD sections 'USAGE AND COMPLETION' and 'MIGRATION'. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Read .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json body.stories and body.nonGoals, compared against HLD §6 Story boundaries and §3/§8 prose.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"DEF s1's acceptance criteria (immutable commit packets with parent/merge provenance and old/new line ranges incl. add/delete/rename/binary, ambiguity reporting, planless taskBasis without inventing tasks, revision-mismatch detection) are represented as fields on sc1's ReviewSubjectV1/CommitPacketV1 (`taskBasis`, `ambiguities`, block `kind`/`oldLines`/`newLines`, `attributionRefs`).","evidence":"DEF ac1-ac4 for s1 (lines 199-240 of the DEF body) each name a requirement that has a literal counterpart field in the sc1 interface sketch in HLD §5.1. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Cross-read DEF s1 acceptanceCriteria against the ReviewSubjectV1/CommitPacketV1 interface sketch in HLD §5.1.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts defines storyRangeDiff at line 446 performing per-unit, per-commit diff assembly (plain vs shared paths, merge-edit folding), matching the HLD's cited reuse seam for Story-attributed patch assembly (citation c2, lines 446-489).","evidence":"grounding.ts:446 `export async function storyRangeDiff(...)` with per-unit loop at lines 470-479 handling shared/merge-edit paths exactly as the DEF/HLD citation describes. [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts]","action":"Read src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts lines 400-480.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts defines codexReviewSessionArgs at lines 138-140 passing `--sandbox read-only`, matching the HLD's claim of existing CLI read-only reviewer-session execution (citation c11).","evidence":"cli-provider.ts:139-140: `export function codexReviewSessionArgs(...) { return ['exec', '--output-schema', schemaPath, '--json', '--sandbox', 'read-only', '-C', cwd, ...modelArgs]; }`. [files: src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts]","action":"Read src/agent/providers/cli-provider.ts lines 125-150.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"src/workflow/review-pipeline/budget.ts's createReviewBudgetPolicy/measureReviewBudget default to a 128,000-token inclusive estimated budget (DEFAULT_REVIEW_CHUNK_TOKENS), matching the HLD's claim 'The default request cap remains the inclusive estimated128K policy with provider-qualified reserves'.","evidence":"budget.ts:13-16 REVIEW_BUDGET_DEFAULTS.totalTokens = DEFAULT_REVIEW_CHUNK_TOKENS; limit.ts:21 `export const DEFAULT_REVIEW_CHUNK_TOKENS = 128_000;`. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/budget.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/limit.ts]","action":"Read src/workflow/review-pipeline/budget.ts lines 1-20 and 86-154, then src/workflow/review-pipeline/limit.ts line 21.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The sc1-sc7 interface names (EvidenceV1, CoverageV1, ReviewLedgerV1, ReviewRuntimePortsV1, InvestigationTurnV1, ReviewRecoveryV1, ReviewCompletionReceiptV1) are genuinely new — no existing type of these names exists anywhere else in the repository that the HLD could be silently duplicating or conflicting with.","evidence":"Grep for `EvidenceV1|ReviewLedgerV1|CoverageV1|ReviewRuntimePortsV1|InvestigationTurnV1` across the repo returns matches only inside the HLD's own artifact/markdown files, not inside any src/ file. [files: docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/HLD.md]","action":"Grepped the whole repo for the new type names.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 'reuse' claim for sc1 is honest about scope: the current CodeReviewSubject (src/workflow/code-review/types.ts) carries only a flat `changedFiles: readonly string[]` list with no per-commit/blob/block identity, so the HLD's 'exact Git commit/blob/block navigation' (CommitPacketV1) is correctly new design, not an already-built capability, as the HLD itself states ('reuse seams, not finished implementations of these proposed contracts').","evidence":"code-review/types.ts:176-198 CodeReviewSubject has only `changedFiles: readonly string[]`, `changeSetAttribution`, `sharedWithExcluded`, `excludedFromScope` — no per-commit parent/blob/block fields exist today. [files: src/workflow/code-review/types.ts]","action":"Read src/workflow/code-review/types.ts CodeReviewSubject interface.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every shared contract's 'Consumed by' list (sc1-sc7, HLD §5) is consistent with the 'Depends on' field on the Story that owns the consuming side (HLD §6), so no Story is left needing a contract it isn't listed as depending on and no contract is consumed by a Story that doesn't own/depend on it.","evidence":"sc1 Consumed by s2-s6 matches s2..s6 each listing sc1 in Depends on; sc3 Consumed by s4-s6 matches s4-s6's Depends on lists; sc4 Consumed by s5-s6 matches; sc5 Consumed by s6 matches; sc6 Consumed by s2-s6 matches. [files: docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/HLD.md]","action":"Cross-checked each shared-contract 'Owner/Consumed by' line against each Story's 'Owns/Depends on' line in HLD §5 and §6.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An integration seam for sc5's 'canonical CR adaptation' already exists (codeReviewArtifactId/buildArtifactId in src/workflow/storage.ts and LifecycleService/createCompletionEvidence in src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts), so the design's claim of a real reuse point for terminal CR publication is grounded rather than hand-waved.","evidence":"storage.ts:382 buildArtifactId, :395 codeReviewArtifactId, :1029 join(... codeReviewArtifactId(...)); repo-lifecycle.ts:27-35 createRepoLifecycle wires History/ArtifactStore/LifecycleService with completion evidence. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts]","action":"Read src/workflow/storage.ts around lines 380-400 and 1020-1035, and src/workflow/artifact-core/repo-lifecycle.ts in full.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing CR-record readers already fail open on unreadable/malformed/unknown-verdict records (never fabricate a block), which supports the HLD's compatibility claim that legacy CR readers keep working once new fields (engine, groundingMode-style discriminants) are added by the successor.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts lines 78-100: a JSON-parse/shape failure or a verdict outside {'pass','warn','block'} both `return { status: 'no-review' }` (fail-open), never a spurious block. [files: src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts]","action":"Read src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts lines 65-101.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing `.insrc/review-runs/<runId>.jsonl` files are plain append-only call-event diagnostics with no checkpoint/accepted-state structure, matching the HLD's claim that 'Existing metadata-only .insrc/review-runs/<runId>.jsonl diagnostics remain content-free and are not recovery checkpoints', so the new durable store at a different path (`investigation-v1/<runId>/`) does not collide with or silently reinterpret the legacy files.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/run-events.ts: `appendReviewRunEvent` just JSON.stringify's a `ReviewCallEvent` and appends it to `.insrc/review-runs/<runId>.jsonl` — no checkpoint, generation or accepted-state fields. [files: src/workflow/code-review/run-events.ts]","action":"Read src/workflow/code-review/run-events.ts in full and globbed .insrc/review-runs/*.jsonl to confirm the path/shape in use.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The prior epic DEF-8315a11f29fd2812 ('Chunked review pipeline for every review'), whose code (code-review-chunk.ts, code-review-gather.ts) the HLD cites, is already approved/built; the HLD does not redesign or re-own that epic's Stories — it treats that code strictly as a cited reuse/replacement candidate and gates its retirement on a later, explicit rollout stage (F) with parity evaluation first.","evidence":"DEF-8315a11f29fd2812.json: `\"status\": \"approved\"`, `\"title\": \"Chunked review pipeline for every review\"`; HLD §3 calls code-review-chunk.ts/gather.ts 'reuse candidates, not the proposed agent investigation loop' and §8 Rollout F states retirement happens only 'after staged accuracy/coverage and recovery validation'. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-8315a11f29fd2812.json]","action":"Read .insrc/artifacts/DEF-8315a11f29fd2812.json status/title and compared to HLD §3 and §8 Rollout stage F / Migration section.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.2","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Within this epic, sc6 is owned by s1 but durably implemented by s4 and composed into production by s6; checked against DEF's own dependsOn graph (s3 dependsOn [s1,s2]; s4 dependsOn [s2,s3]) this split introduces no backward dependency of an earlier Story (s3) on a later one (s4), consistent with the HLD's explicit claim that 's3 does not acquire a forbidden backwards dependency on s4'.","evidence":"DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json body.stories s3.dependsOn=['s1','s2'], s4.dependsOn=['s2','s3'] — s4 depends on s3, never the reverse, matching the HLD's port-split rationale in §5.6 and §8 'Ordering rationale'. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Checked DEF s3/s4 dependsOn arrays against the HLD's sc6/Story-boundary narrative.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's completion verdict vocabulary ('pass'|'warn'|'block' on ReviewCompletionReceiptV1) reuses the existing ReviewVerdict/Severity types verbatim rather than inventing a parallel verdict language, as the HLD itself asserts ('Existing severity/confidence folding and independent-party rules remain authoritative').","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/types.ts imports `Severity, ReviewVerdict` from '../review/types.js' and CodeReviewBody.verdict is typed `ReviewVerdict`, the same union the HLD's ReviewCompletionReceiptV1.verdict reuses. [files: src/workflow/code-review/types.ts]","action":"Read src/workflow/code-review/types.ts imports and CodeReviewBody.verdict field, compared to HLD §5.5 ReviewCompletionReceiptV1.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The HLD's indexed-impact failure handling ('A missing graph entity, stale index, unmatched snapshot version or empty caller result is not proof of no impact') is grounded in the real freshness module's existing distinction between staleFiles and unindexedFiles and its fail-safe default (a selection-read failure is kept stale rather than marked fresh), which is the detectable failure surface the new impact capability would build on.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts lines 71-100: a `selection` read that throws sets `selection = 'selected'` and `listable = false`, keeping the file stale rather than silently treating it as fresh/no-impact. [files: src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts]","action":"Read src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts lines 35-100.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"At HLD granularity the design states a coherent test strategy per DEF constraint k8/s6-ac3 (deterministic/mock providers for routine tests, separately authorized live comparisons, independently adjudicated fixtures before default adoption) and enables per-Story testability (e.g. s3's in-memory foundational ports as 'test scaffolding' ahead of s4's durable store), even though it correctly defers concrete AC-to-test-case mapping to the LLD/PLAN stage per this project's own workflow convention.","evidence":"HLD §7 Non-functional 'Performance': 'Use deterministic/mock providers for routine tests; measure authorized live comparisons against recorded baselines before claiming savings.'; §6.3 Story s3: 'In-memory ports are test scaffolding while production selection remains disabled until s4/s6'; §8 Rollout stage F requires 'parity/quality evaluation' before adoption, directly operationalizing DEF s6-ac3. [files: docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/HLD.md, .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Read HLD §7 Non-functional targets, §6.3 Story s3 boundary text, and §8 Rollout stage F, and matched them to DEF s6 acceptanceCriteria ac3.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":16,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-28T08:08:11.924Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
