12762	{"artifactId":"HLD-c32aa60534232f36","entry":{"id":"review-ba1bf02862be57da3478300c9a90deb5","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-28T11:30:43.345Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every DEF Story (s1-s6, DEF-c32aa60534232f36) has a matching HLD Story with the same shared-contract ownership and dependency ordering (s1->sc1/sc6, s2->sc2, s3->sc3, s4->sc4, s5->sc5, s6->sc7), and no DEF non-goal (new usage warehouse/pricing engine/model catalog, changed severity policy, auto-approval, guaranteed exact token savings) is introduced by the HLD.","evidence":"DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json body.stories[s1..s6].dependsOn exactly mirrors HLD §6 Story boundaries' Depends-on lists (s2:sc1/sc6; s3:sc1/sc2/sc6; s4:sc1/sc2/sc3/sc6; s5:sc1..sc4/sc6; s6:sc1..sc6), and DEF body.nonGoals ('Introduce a new token-usage warehouse, model catalog or client-specific delivery-board UI', 'Change severity policy... or automatically approve work') are respected verbatim by HLD's USAGE AND COMPLETION section ('No new warehouse, pricing engine or usage arrays... existing severity/confidence and human approval/override gates remain authoritative'). [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json]","action":"Read DEF-c32aa60534232f36.json body.stories and body.nonGoals and compared against HLD §5/§6.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts's storyRangeDiff already avoids a generic base..HEAD diff fallback and instead assembles per-unit (per-commit) diffs with explicit provenance when a path was also touched by a merge or a left-out commit, as the HLD's 'reuse seam, not a finished implementation' claim states.","evidence":"grounding.ts:432-489 doc comment and body: 'Paths no merge touched get one net base..HEAD diff limited to them. A path a merge also changed gets, instead, the diff of each Story unit that touched it... so no merged-in line reaches the reviewer... EVERY path takes the per-unit route' when units came from story-trailer attribution. [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts]","action":"Read storyRangeDiff (lines ~432-489).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts's resolveCodeReviewSubject already treats a missing/unapproved LLD or PLAN as an optional null field (mode derived from presence) rather than a failure, and declines only with 'no-build-record' when no changed files can be derived — matching the HLD's description of this as an existing reuse seam.","evidence":"subject.ts:133-172: each of requireApprovedLld/requireApprovedPlan is wrapped in its own try/catch mapping ArtifactMissingError/ArtifactNotApprovedError to null; the only decline path returns {ok:false, reason:'no-build-record'} on an undefined range base or an empty changedFiles set. [files: src/workflow/code-review/subject.ts]","action":"Read resolveCodeReviewSubject body.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed new types/capabilities (InvestigationContinuationV1, InvestigationTurnV1, ReviewRuntimePortsV1, BlockCheckpointReceiptV1, queryChangedEntityCallers, the .insrc/review-runs/investigation-v1/ store) do not already exist anywhere in src/, so labelling them 'new' is accurate.","evidence":"grep for 'investigation-v1|InvestigationContinuationV1|InvestigationTurnV1|ReviewRuntimePortsV1|BlockCheckpointReceiptV1' across src/ returned zero matches; grep for 'queryChangedEntityCallers' also returned zero matches (only the existing findCallers/traversal primitives exist, in src/db/graph/edges.ts and traversal.ts). [files: src/db/graph/edges.ts, src/db/graph/traversal.ts]","action":"Grep for the proposed new identifiers and for the existing findCallers primitive.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The HLD's claim that usage adapters should 'reuse src/workflow/usage/types.ts... the existing five normalized counter buckets' is accurate: NormalizedCounters already has exactly five fields.","evidence":"src/workflow/usage/types.ts:32-38 defines NormalizedCounters with exactly inputUncachedTokens, cacheReadTokens, cacheWriteTokens, outputTokens, reasoningTokens. [files: src/workflow/usage/types.ts]","action":"Read the NormalizedCounters type definition.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding a new coverageRef field to the persisted CodeReviewBody (sc5's ReviewCompletionReceiptV1 maps into the existing CR artifact) is a backward-compatible additive change, consistent with the repo's established pattern of optional fields that keep older records valid.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/types.ts's CodeReviewBody already carries several optional additive fields (fallbackReason?, changeSetAttribution?, pipelineCalls?, outOfScope?, lowered?) each documented as 'absent on records written before this field existed' / 'byte-identical to one written before this field existed' — the same pattern the HLD's sc5/completion section relies on for compatibility. [files: src/workflow/code-review/types.ts]","action":"Read CodeReviewBody and its optional-field comments.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing .insrc/review-runs/<runId>.jsonl diagnostics (appendReviewRunEvent / ReviewCallEvent) are metadata-only and content-free, and are not a recovery checkpoint mechanism, as the HLD claims when distinguishing them from the new durable runtime store.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifact-core's appendReviewRunEvent appends one ReviewCallEvent JSON line per call; ReviewCallEvent (src/workflow/review-pipeline/call-events.ts:13-30) carries only dimension/stage/role/attempt/transport/policyVersion/budget/durationMs/errorCode/timing fields -- no prompt text, evidence or answer content, and no sequence/digest fields that would let it reconstruct or replay accepted state. [files: src/workflow/code-review/run-events.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/call-events.ts]","action":"Read appendReviewRunEvent and the ReviewCallEvent interface.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The HLD's Story s3 (owns sc3 InvestigationContinuationV1, including ReviewBlockProgressV1/BlockCheckpointReceiptV1 — a new controller continuation/progress-acknowledgment protocol over insrc_code_review_step) and Story s6 (owns sc7 ReviewClientStatusV1, described as 'equivalent MCP/daemon/controller start/status/resume/cancel adapters') do not redesign or collide with any contract the approved-but-unbuilt sibling Story S005 of the chunked-review-pipeline-every-review epic (8315a11f) already owns over the same insrc_code_review_step/insrc_review_step MCP surface.","evidence":"LLD-8315a11f29fd2812-s5.json has lifecycle.status 'approved' (meta.lifecycle.status=\"approved\"), and HLD-8315a11f29fd2812.json's own HLD (§4.7 sc7, §5.5 S005) states S005 'Owns: sc7' -- 'The two controller steps' use of the job, and the MCP boundary that admits it: the new answers phase in the insrc_review_step and insrc_code_review_step input schemas in src/mcp/server.ts... one frame shape both controller steps use for every new controller review' (EmitCallsFrame / AnswersInput keyed by ReviewCall.callId). There is no BUILD-8315a11f29fd2812-s5 record yet (only BUILD-...-s1/-s2/-s3 exist), so this approved contract is still pending build, not retired. The new HLD (c32aa60534232f36) never mentions this sibling epic, Story, or its sc7 contract anywhere in its text, Rollout, or References; its own Rollout §F explicitly scopes retirement to 'predecessor code-review chunk/gather requirements' only (S002/S003), leaving S005's controller-frame ownership of the identical MCP entrypoints completely unaddressed while s3/s6 independently define a second, incompatible continuation/status protocol (InvestigationTurnV1/InvestigationReplyV1/ReviewBlockProgressV1/ReviewClientStatusV1) for the same code-review entrypoint. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-8315a11f29fd2812-s5.json, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/HLD.md]","action":"Read LLD-8315a11f29fd2812-s5.json lifecycle status, cross-referenced against HLD-8315a11f29fd2812's §4.7/§5.5 Story-S005/sc7 ownership text and against the new HLD's full text/Rollout for any mention of this sibling epic/Story; found none.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The HLD's error-handling stance (fail-open on unreadable/unknown-shape records, explicit unresolved/unverified dispositions rather than fabricated pass, stale/missing index treated as unresolved rather than proof of no-impact) is consistent with the existing, already-shipped fail-open patterns in the code-review subsystem it says it builds on.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts's enforceCodeReviewGate already fails open to 'no-review' on an unreadable JSON file or an unrecognized verdict ('never manufactures a block from a record it cannot read' / 'never a spurious block'), and src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts already marks a file stale rather than silently passing it when its selection read throws ('keep it stale, request nothing'). The HLD's analogous rules (a torn tail/corrupt blob is 'detected, never accepted as complete'; a missing graph entity or stale index 'is not proof of no impact') follow the same existing fail-safe-toward-caution convention rather than contradicting it. [files: src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts, src/workflow/code-review/freshness.ts]","action":"Read enforceCodeReviewGate and computeCodeReviewFreshness for their existing fail-open/fail-stale conventions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The HLD provides an explicit mapping from the DEF's acceptance criteria (s1 ac1-ac4, s2 ac1-ac3, s3 ac1-ac5, s4 ac1-ac5, s5 ac1-ac4, s6 ac1-ac4 -- roughly 25 criteria) to planned tests, following the convention already used by other HLDs in this repo.","evidence":"This HLD has no section mapping acceptance criteria to planned tests anywhere in its text, Story boundaries, or Rollout -- only general, qualitative test-strategy prose ('Use deterministic/mock providers for routine tests... authorize live comparisons separately', 'Test one session reviewing multiple blocks, crash after an acknowledged block...'). By contrast, sibling approved HLDs in this same repo explicitly carry this mapping, e.g. docs/epics/manage-saved-temporary-data-connections-E20261021484fcef7/HLD.md:59 ('Planned acceptance-to-test mapping (each is a test obligation, not an implemented test)' followed by per-story/ac rows) and docs/epics/understand-changes-before-committing-E20261017670419c4/HLD.md:61 ('Planned verification matrix: these are acceptance tests to implement, not test results. Every row is owned by the named story'). None of this HLD's ~25 acceptance criteria is traceable to a named planned test or test owner anywhere in the document. [files: docs/epics/manage-saved-temporary-data-connections-E20261021484fcef7/HLD.md, docs/epics/understand-changes-before-committing-E20261017670419c4/HLD.md]","action":"Searched this HLD's full text for an AC-to-test mapping (none found) and grepped sibling HLD.md files in docs/epics for the equivalent section to confirm it is an established, followable convention at this design stage, not an LLD-only concern.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":1,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-28T11:30:43.345Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
